      "slug": "diamond-mesh",
      "term": "Diamond mesh",
      "definition": "A two-row repeat where a treble, ch-2 space, treble creates open squares that offset between rows to form a diamond or trellis pattern."
    },
    {
      "slug": "turning-chain",
      "term": "Turning chain",
      "definition": "Five chains at the start of a diamond mesh row, counting as a tr and ch-2 space."
    },
